<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tvrtko I of Bosnia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1338–1391</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Stephen Tvrtko I</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tvrtko I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a>, of the Kotromanić dynasty, ruled Bosnia as ban from 1353 and in 1377 was crowned king at Mile, claiming the Serbian crown through descent from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nemanjic-dynasty">Nemanjić dynasty</a>. He extended his rule over western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, Zachlumia and much of the Dalmatian coast, making Bosnia briefly the strongest state in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balkans">Balkans</a>. His kingdom weakened soon after his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tvrtko-i-of-bosnia.jpg" alt="Tvrtko I of Bosnia" width="320" height="318" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tvrtko I of Bosnia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seal_of_Tvrtko_I_of_Bosnia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
